          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In general, the term ‘cross product’ is used for any operation denoted by the symbol ‘
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo ×
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \times
            ’, such as
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/cartesian+product"} cartesian product
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+product"} direct product
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Tychonoff+product"} Tychonoff product
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/product"} product in a category
          %p
            However, there is another completely different context, used in the elementary analysis of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/vector+spaces"} vector spaces
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternions"} quaternions
            as a binary operation on
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msup
                      %mi ℝ
                      %mn 3
                    %mo ≃
                    %mi Im
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi ℍ
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^3 \simeq Im(\mathbb{H})
          %p
            None of this should be confused with the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/crossed+product"} crossed product
            of of a
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+action"} Hopf action
          %h2#definitions Definitions
          %h3#classical Classical
          %p
            The
            %strong classical cross product
            on the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Cartesian+space"} Cartesian space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^3
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bilinear+function"} bilinear function
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 3
                  %mo ×
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 3
                  %mo →
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (-) \times (-)\colon \mathbb{R}^3 \times \mathbb{R}^3 \to \mathbb{R}^3
          %p given by
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi b
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi d
                  %mo ,
                  %mi e
                  %mo ,
                  %mi f
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mi f
                  %mo −
                  %mi c
                  %mi e
                  %mo ,
                  %mi c
                  %mi d
                  %mo −
                  %mi a
                  %mi f
                  %mo ,
                  %mi a
                  %mi e
                  %mo −
                  %mi b
                  %mi d
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a,b,c) \times (d,e,f) = (b f - c e, c d - a f, a e - b d) .
          %p
            This operation is invariant under
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orthogonal+group"} orthogonal transformations
            and there is nothing special here about the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            = succeed "-dimensional" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 3
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation"} oriented
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+product+space"} inner product space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            over any
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/field"} field
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi V
                  %mo ×
                  %mi V
                  %mo →
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (-) \times (-)\colon V \times V \to V
          %p
            given, upon choosing any oriented orthonormal basis for
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/free+module"} free module
            of rank
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3
            over any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/commutative+ring"} commutative ring
            (or arguably a non-commutative
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/rig"} rig
          %h3#binary Binary
          %p We have already, trivially, generalized the cross product to other ground fields. One way to generalise it to other dimensions is to identify characteristic features as a bilinear operation and see what operations in other dimensions have these.
          %p
            In this vein, a
            %strong binary cross product
            on any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+product+space"} inner product space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            is a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bilinear+function"} bilinear function
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ×
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %mi V
                  %mo ×
                  %mi V
                  %mo →
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  (-) \times (-)\colon V \times V \to V
          %p
            such that for all
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo ∈
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y\in V
            we have
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                Alternation:
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ×
                        %mi x
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \times x = 0
            %li
              %p
                Orthgonality:
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ×
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \times y
                is orthogonal to both
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x
                and
                = succeed ";" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi y
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} y
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ×
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo =
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi x
                        %mo ×
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo ⋅
                        %mi y
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \cdot (x \times y) = (x \times y) \cdot y = 0
            %li
              %p
                Area:
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi x
                        %mo ×
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mo =
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi x
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|x \times y\|} = {\|x\|} {\|y\|}
                if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi x
                      %mo ,
                      %mi y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x, y
                are orthogonal.
          %p
            From these, we can prove a more general formula for
            = succeed ":" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi x
                      %mo ×
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|x \times y\|}
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi x
                      %mo ×
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mn 2
                  %mo =
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi x
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mn 2
                  %msup
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mi y
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mn 2
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi y
                  %msup
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mn 2
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|x \times y\|}^2 = {\|x\|}^2 {\|y\|}^2 - (x \cdot y)^2 ,
          %p or equivalently
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mi x
                    %mo ×
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %mo =
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                    %mi sin
                    %mo ∠
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi x
                    %mo ,
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} |
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|x \times y\|} = {\|x\|} {\|y\|} {|\sin\angle(x,y)|} .
          %p
            (Using the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/polarization+identity"} polarization identity
            to express
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi y
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \cdot y
            in terms of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mi x
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \|x\|
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \|y\|
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %mi x
                  %mo +
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \|x + y\|
            or
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %mi x
                    %mo −
                    %mi y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \|x - y\|
          %p Conversely, using this more general area formula, we can prove both the restricted area formula and alternation, so that only orthogonality is needed as a separate axiom.
          %p
            We then have over the
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                In
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
                or
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi x
                        %mo ×
                        %mi y
                        %mo ≔
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \times y \coloneqq 0
            %li
              %p
                In dimension
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 3
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3
            %li
              %p
                In dimension
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 7
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 7
            %li
              %p In any other finite dimension, there are no binary cross products at all.
          %p
            These cross products exist over any base field, but as far as I know there may be additional cross products over some fields in dimensions greater than
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 7
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 7
            dimensions becomes the claim that the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+variety"} algebraic variety
            of these inner products has dimension greater than
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 2
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
          %p
            Binary cross products are closely related to
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normed+division+algebras"} normed division algebras
            (NDAs). Given a normed division algebra
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi A
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi Im
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi A
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Im(A)
            inherits an inner product from
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            and gains a cross product as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi x
                  %mo ×
                  %mi y
                  %mo ≔
                  %mi Im
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi x
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mfrac
                    %mn 1
                    %mn 2
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} [
                  %mi x
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ]
                  %mo =
                  %mi x
                  %mi y
                  %mo +
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi y
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} x \times y \coloneqq Im(x y) = \frac{1}{2}[x,y] = x y + x \cdot y .
          %p
            Conversely, given an inner product space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            with a binary cross product, the orthogonal
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/direct+sum"} direct sum
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \oplus V
            becomes a NDA as
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mo ,
                  %mi x
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi b
                  %mo ,
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi a
                  %mi b
                  %mo −
                  %mi x
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi y
                  %mo ,
                  %mi a
                  %mi y
                  %mo +
                  %mi b
                  %mi x
                  %mo +
                  %mi x
                  %mo ×
                  %mi y
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (a,x) (b,y) = (a b - x \cdot y, a y + b x + x \times y) ,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi K
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K
            is the ground field. (Compare the relationship between complex
            = succeed "-algebras" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo *
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} *
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Jordan--Lie+algebras"} Jordan–Lie algebras
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi A
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} A
            is
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                  %mo ⊕
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V \oplus V
            instead of
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi K
                    %mo ⊕
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} K \oplus V
            = succeed ".)" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi V
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
          %p
            By
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hurwitz+theorem"} Hurwitz's theorem
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            are
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            itself (the
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
            (the
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℍ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{H}
            (the
            = succeed ")," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/quaternions"} quaternions
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi 𝕆
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{O}
            (the
            = succeed ")." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/octonions"} octonions
          %p
            By one of the deeper strands of mathematics, this classification of something as innocent-looking as cross-products is closely related not just to the existence of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/normed+division+algebras"} normed division algebras
            over the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+numbers"} real numbers
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/parallelizable+manifold"} parallelizable
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/n-spheres"} n-spheres
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/real+spin+representations"} real spin representations
            (see also at
            = succeed ")," do
              %em
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/supersymmetry+and+division+algebras"} supersymmetry and division algebras
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+groups+of+spheres"} homotopy groups of spheres
            of
            = succeed ";" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Hopf+invariant+one"} Hopf invariant one
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "Hopf+invariant+one#RelationToHSpaceStructureAndNormedDivisionAlgebras"} there
          %h3#counary
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi n
                  %mo −
                  %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
            \-ary
          %p
            Given an
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/orientation"} oriented
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+product+space"} inner product space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            of finite
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/dimension"} dimension
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/volume"} volume
            of an
            = succeed "-" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/tuple"} tuple
            of vectors. (See also
            = succeed ".)" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/volume+form"} volume form
            = succeed "-ary" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi n
                    %mo −
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n - 1)
            %strong co-unary cross product
            of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                  %mo −
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n - 1
            vectors as a multilinear operation
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ⨉
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo →
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} &amp;#10761;\colon V^{n - 1} \to V
          %p such that
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ⋅
                  %mi ⨉
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo =
                  %mi vol
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mn 0
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mn 1
                  %mo ,
                  %mi …
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_0 \cdot &amp;#10761;(v_1,\ldots,v_{n-1}) = vol(v_0,v_1,\ldots,v_{n-1})
          %p
            always. There is exactly one such cross product on any such
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            (so two if we start with an unoriented inner product space).
          %p
            In
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 3
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 3
            dimensions, this also recovers the classical cross product. In
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 2
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
            dimensions, this produces a
            %strong unary cross product
            given by
            = succeed ";" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo ×
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi a
                    %mo ,
                    %mi b
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mo =
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi b
                    %mo ,
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                    %mi a
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\times}(a,b) = (b,-a)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            dimension, this is a nullary operation (a constant) whose value is the positive normal vector
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
          %h3#vectorvalued Vector-valued
          %p
            Generalizing all of the above, let a
            %strong vector-valued cross product
            on any
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/inner+product+space"} inner product space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            be a multilinear function
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ⨉
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                  %msup
                    %mi V
                    %mi k
                  %mo →
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} &amp;#10761;\colon V^k \to V
          %p
            for some
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/natural+number"} natural number
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            (called the
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/arity"} arity
          %ol
            %li
              %p
                Alternation:
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ⨉
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} &amp;#10761;(v_1,\ldots,v_k) = 0
                if
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mi i
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mi j
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_i = v_j
                for some
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi i
                        %mo ≠
                        %mi j
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} i \ne j
            %li
              %p
                Orthgonality:
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi ⨉
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mn 1
                      %mo ,
                      %mi …
                      %mo ,
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} &amp;#10761;(v_1,\ldots,v_k)
                is orthogonal to each
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mi i
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_i
            %li
              %p
                Area:
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %mi ⨉
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mi …
                        %mo ,
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                      %mo =
                      %msub
                        %mo{:lspace => "thinmathspace", :rspace => "thinmathspace"} ∏
                        %mi i
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                        %msub
                          %mi v
                          %mi i
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} ‖
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} {\|&amp;#10761;(v_1,\ldots,v_k)\|} = \prod_i {\|v_i\|}
                if the
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msub
                        %mi v
                        %mi i
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_i
                are mutually orthogonal.
          %p
            We can again extend (3) to get the magnitude of the cross product of any
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            vectors; its square is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/determinant"} determinant
            of the matrix whose
            = succeed "th" do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mi i
                    %mo ,
                    %mi j
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (i,j)
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mi i
                  %mo ⋅
                  %msub
                    %mi v
                    %mi j
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} v_i \cdot v_j
            (the
            = succeed ")," do
              %span.newWikiWord
                Gram determinant
                %a{:href => "/nlab/new/Gram+determinant"} ?
          %p
            Then for an inner product space
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi V
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
            over
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℝ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}
            of finite dimension
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                If
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = 0
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/unit+vector"} unit vector
                of
                = succeed ":" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi V
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} V
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 0
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 1
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 2
                (of which
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 2
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2n
                are compatible with a given basis).
            %li
              %p
                If
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = 1
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mi ℝ
                        %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^n
                as as
                = succeed "-fold" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n/2
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internal+direct+sum"} internal direct sum
                of
                = succeed "-dimensional" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 0
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo =
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 2
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo ≥
                      %mn 4
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \geq 4
                is even (of which
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %msup
                        %mn 2
                        %mrow
                          %mi n
                          %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                          %mn 2
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo −
                      %mn 1
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo !
                      %mo !
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 2^{n/2}(n-1)!!
                are compatible with a given basis), and none when
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                is odd.
            %li
              %p
                If
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo =
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = 2
                %a{:href => "#binary"} above
                for binary cross products: one (always
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 0, 1
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo =
                        %mn 3
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 3
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn 480
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 480
                are compatible with a given basis) when
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo =
                        %mn 7
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 7
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ≠
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 3
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 7
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \ne 0, 1, 3, 7
            %li
              %p
                If
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo =
                        %mn 3
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = 3
                = succeed ")" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 0, 1, 2
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo =
                        %mn 4
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 4
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo =
                        %mn 8
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 8
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo ≠
                        %mn 0
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 1
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 2
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 4
                        %mo ,
                        %mn 8
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \ne 0, 1, 2, 4, 8
            %li
              %p
                If
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 4
                        %mo ≤
                        %mi k
                        %mo &lt;
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 4 \leq k \lt n - 1
            %li
              %p
                If
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo =
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = n - 1
                %a{:href => "#counary"} above
                for
                = succeed "-ary" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo −
                        %mn 1
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n-1)
            %li
              %p
                If
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo =
                        %mi n
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = n
            %li
              %p
                If
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ≥
                        %mi n
                        %mo +
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \geq n + 1
                = succeed ")." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0
          %p
            Or organized by dimension (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi n
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
            ) rather than arity (
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi k
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k
            ):
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                If
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 0
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi k
                      %mo =
                      %mn 0
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = 0
                and one cross product (always zero) when
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \geq 1
            %li
              %p
                If
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 1
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = 0
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = 1
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \geq 2
            %li
              %p
                If
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo =
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 2
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = 0
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = 1
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo =
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = 2
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo ≥
                        %mn 3
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k \geq 3
            %li
              %p
                If
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi n
                        %mo =
                        %mn 3
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 3
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo =
                        %mn 0
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = 0
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo =
                        %mn 1
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = 1
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo =
                        %mn 2
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = 2
                = succeed "," do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mi k
                        %mo =
                        %mn 3
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} k = 3
                = succeed "." do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
